{"kind":"artifact","text":"SKILL.md at exact d4726958c7d3fc763e734e43b42be0da40e2daa3 on request/skill-simplify, under promise git:sha1…a431970 on request git:sha1…205421b\n\nSKILL.md carries the loop and says to use it lightly; AGENTS.md carries only what this repository adds; architecture.md records the contract that moved.\n\nRepair of the three blocking findings in verdict 7d3ef0e5, on the same request\nand promise. The outcome, conditions, performer, destination and authority are\nunchanged.\n\n**Finding 1, the unreflected contract change.** docs/reference/architecture.md\nis updated in this same head and its artifact is published here. The AGENTS.md\nrow now says that page carries what this repository adds on top of SKILL.md\nand names the rules it deliberately repeats, and that the three review\nconclusions live in SKILL.md. The SKILL.md row now names those three\nconclusions. The Review rule no longer says AGENTS.md adds the security and\nsimplification checks or that SKILL.md does not carry repository policies; it\nsays SKILL.md carries all three because they are how any workroom reviews an\nimplementation, and AGENTS.md carries only what is local here. The reviewer\noffered both directions and took neither; this is the direction the request\nasked for and the one the head was already going.\n\n**Finding 2, the licence paragraph.** Rewritten to say what the boundary does.\nA stale basis is admitted and recorded, so re-anchor and carry on rather than\nstall over it; a retired one refuses, so repoint it before you file; between\ntwo the boundary would both admit, cite the one you can defend and move on.\nThe claims the reviewer struck are gone: no reviewer safety net, no cheap\nre-anchoring, no standard softer than the closing rule. The verified ground is\ninternal/app/admission.go:241-272, where judgeDeadBases refuses a retired\nbasis and names --allow-dead-basis, which :238-240 says grants nothing, while\na stale basis is admitted and recorded.\n\n**Finding