er `status.` prefix resolved to nothing. `gs state`, `gs batch`,\n`gs ratify` and `gs supersede` are linked to their pages and carry the\n`--no-preflight` escape hatch, so the rule the step-list dropped is reachable.\n\"Or through supersession\" is restored as the second way work closes without\nlanding. The two bare directory links stay: the four act pages are now linked\ndirectly, which is what the reviewer said the link substitution rests on.\n\nConditions, at this head.\n\n1. Verified against the code, not from memory. Every command and flag the page\nnames exists in cmd/gs at d4726958: work --next, wait, status, inspect,\npromise, reassign-if-unclaimed with its flags before the request, artifact\n(--head --promise --report --rests-on --text), review-request (--head --to\n--replace), review (--artifact --promise --checkout --verdict --text-file),\nland (--approval --checkout --text --cleanup), and state, batch, ratify and\nsupersede with --no-preflight. `gs presence` is not a CLI command and the page\nclaims none. All twenty-one document links resolve, including the three\nanchors.\n\n2. Shorter. SKILL.md is 212 lines and 1466 words against 213 and 1499;\nAGENTS.md is 40 lines and 275 words against 100 and 756; the pair went from\n2255 words to 1741. The repairs cost four lines and twenty-seven words against\nthe reviewed head, which the reviewer measured at 208 and 1439. Every refusal\nlist removed from a step is covered in the linked page: promise.md:63-69,\nartifact.md:79-92 with the changed-path warning at :106,\nreview-request.md:66-73, review.md:148-165 and :34, land.md:84-99, and\nmerge.md:586 for the retirements a merge may make. No step lost a rule.\n\n3. The drift is resolved towards SKILL.md, and architecture.md now says so.\n\n4. `go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/...` and `make test` both green at\nexactly d4726958, exit 0; docset ran uncached at 38.7s standalone and again\nat 40.0s inside the full suite, internal/workroom at 7.0s. The packages reported from cache\nare byte-identical to the fresh run at 3049d18b, where cmd/gs took 459.8s;\nonly three Markdown files differ between those heads.\n\n5. One artifact per changed path, all three on this promise, resting on the\neleven behaviour bases the page cites.","body":{"commit":"d4726958c7d3fc763e734e43b42be0da40e2daa3","path":"SKILL.md"}}